cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Runtime Visibility Limits of Bias Probes for Quantum Error-Mitigated Selection: code, protocol and results"
authors:
  - family-names: "Liu"
    given-names: "Zhen-Jun"
abstract: >-
  Code, protocol, results and paper for a preregistered fixed-budget noisy-simulation
  study of when a runtime bias probe can detect that a quantum error-mitigated
  selection decision is wrong. Decision-level results are noisy simulation; an
  exploratory readout test was run on one IBM Quantum device. Source code and tests are
  MIT licensed; documentation and results are licensed under CC BY 4.0.
repository-code: "https://github.com/Raina-ya/bias-probe-visibility"
url: "https://github.com/Raina-ya/bias-probe-visibility"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - "quantum error mitigation"
  - "zero-noise extrapolation"
  - "bias detection"
  - "preregistration"
  - "fixed-budget comparison"
  - "QAOA"
  - "simulation"
